#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:0
msgid ""
"Install Ubuntu Desktop 26.04 LTS on your laptop or PC from a USB stick using "
"the graphical installer, including disk setup and encryption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:8
msgid "Topics: Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:12
msgid "Install Ubuntu Desktop"
msgstr "安裝 Ubuntu Desktop"

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:14
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"Original source: <https://discourse.ubuntu.com/t/install-ubuntu-desktop/"
"25312/>\n"
"Original author: Oliver Smith <oliversmith@canonical.com>\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:19
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we'll download and install Ubuntu Desktop 26.04 LTS on "
"your laptop or PC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:21
msgid ""
"If you've never installed an operating system, don't worry: Ubuntu makes the "
"process very easy. You'll encounter a guided installer that will ask you a "
"couple of questions. Whenever you're not sure what to pick, you can just "
"select the default option, which ensures that you end up with a fully usable "
"Ubuntu installation. No deep technical knowledge is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:23
msgid "What you'll need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:25
msgid "A laptop or PC with at least 25GB of storage space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:27
msgid "A flash drive, 8GB or above recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:30
msgid "Will Ubuntu work on my computer?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:32
msgid ""
"While Ubuntu works on a wide range of devices, it's best to use a device "
"listed on the [Ubuntu certified hardware](https://ubuntu.com/certified?"
"q=&category=Laptop&category=Desktop&limit=20) page. These devices have been "
"tested and confirmed to work well with Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:34
msgid ""
"If you can't see your device there, you can always just {ref}`try-ubuntu-"
"desktop` and check if everything works as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/apple-silicon-disclaimer.txt:2
msgid ""
"If you want to run Ubuntu on **Apple Silicon** hardware, such as recent Macs "
"using M1 CPUs or later, refer instead to the [Ubuntu Asahi](https://"
"ubuntuasahi.org/) community project, which isn't supported by Canonical. The "
"hardware support might be limited and depends on your specific machine. For "
"example, Ubuntu Asahi 25.10 only runs on systems with M1 and M2 CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/apple-silicon-disclaimer.txt:4
msgid ""
"You can also install Ubuntu in a virtual machine on top of your current "
"system using [Multipass](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/multipass/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:39
msgid ""
"For guidance on installing Ubuntu on platforms based on architectures other "
"than x86 (including **ARM** or **RISC-V** boards, such as **Raspberry Pi**), "
"see {external+hw:doc}`index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:43
msgid "Back up your data"
msgstr "備份您的資料"

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:45
msgid ""
"If you're installing Ubuntu on a PC or laptop that you've used previously, "
"back up your data before you start the installation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:47
msgid ""
"Move any **files** that you want to keep to another storage device, such as "
"an external disk or a USB drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:49
msgid ""
"To back up your **web browser**, connect your browser to an online account, "
"such as a Firefox account or a Google account. After the Ubuntu "
"installation, your browser synchronizes your data when you log into your "
"account. Note that the Safari browser doesn't work on Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:51
msgid ""
"Back up your files from the **USB flash drive**. The drive will be erased."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-ubuntu-desktop.md:54
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"The docs/reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt file is reused between the live "
"system tutorial and the installation tutorial.\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt:2
msgid "Download an Ubuntu image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt:4
msgid ""
"Get the Ubuntu installation image from the [Download Ubuntu Desktop](https://"
"ubuntu.com/download/desktop) page. Save it to a memorable location on your "
"PC. The downloaded file is called `ubuntu-26.04-desktop-amd64.iso` or "
"similar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt:6
msgid ""
"![The Download Ubuntu Desktop page](/images/download-an-ubuntu-image.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt:6
msgid "The Download Ubuntu Desktop page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt:9
msgid "Create a bootable USB stick"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt:11
msgid ""
"Write the downloaded Ubuntu image to a USB stick to create the installation "
"media. This is not the same as copying the downloaded image file: you have "
"to use special software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt:14
msgid "This will erase your USB stick. Back up your files first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt:17
msgid ""
"The application that we'll use depends on the system that you're currently "
"using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/boot-ubuntu-from-usb.txt:0
msgid "On Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

